{"kind":"artifact","text":"The public API an application outside this module imports to run on the gitseq kernel, at exact head 2867e08818c68e9144bac947bb70f122f075c927 on request/chess-item3-public-api, rebased onto main 5a9529b3. Four acts and no projection: Init creates a sequence and binds it to the application for life, recording the binding as the log's first record so the key that signed it is the binding authority from then on; Open verifies the sequence and only then hands it back to the application it is bound to, refusing anything else as verifiable but uninterpretable; Append signs one act with a caller's key and gives it a position; Records returns the verified ordered record stream. The outside application holds its own fold. No roster and no admission allowlist, because its actors are keys; kernel bounds and a bounded sequencer queue still apply. Two of the three defects the previous review found are closed here. Open reads the binding out of the exact frontier the kernel just verified rather than verifying one frontier and asking the ref again a moment later, so an appender racing the open can no longer bind a workspace by a history nobody checked. Append computes the payload tree's object identity with gitstore.HashPayloadTree instead of writing it, leaving the single write to the kernel after its size, field, and signature checks pass: a refused act now leaves no unreachable objects behind, and a valid act stops writing the same tree twice. Conditions met: go test -count=1 ./... is clean at this exact head, 26 packages ok including the out-of-module import proof that builds a second Go module against this checkout, the docset gates, and cmd/gs; go vet ./... is clean. New regressions here prove a refused act writes no objects and that a repository whose ceiling exceeds the signed read limit still opens. Each of the three fixes was mutation-checked: reverting it makes its own test fail.","body":{"branch":"request/chess-item3-public-api","commit":"2867e08818c68e9144bac947bb70f122f075c927","path":"host"}}